{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/781227-changlings-and-trad-mages","id":781227,"title":"Changlings and Trad Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-06T11:59:42-08:00","id":781227,"title":"Changlings and Trad Mages","content":"Basically, how often do you get these groups together? They've got the least reasons to fear/loath each other of any of the major splats and plenty to gain from alliance. so, do you get them together, or keep them apart.<br /> <br /> Myself? Let me say that many of my Hermetics are Bani-Merinita with fay blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:45:44-08:00","id":781271,"title":"","content":"Honestly, given that Freeholds are also treasured places of mystical power, my inclination would be to imagine that changelings are, on the whole, almost as distrustful of mages as Garou and Fera. Mysticks are always out looking for a source of power to siphon off for their own purposes, and are bad news if they're sniffing around your place. The main difference being that changelings are more likely to try trickery and misdirection than just twisting and pulling their adversaries' heads off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:48:23-08:00","id":781274,"title":"","content":"Depends on the game and the kind of characters playing. Technocratic games: virtually never. Tradition games: sometimes with only one major character really turning into a semi regular guest star. When I play a cultist or Verbena I usually have fae blood, I even made an Etherite once with the merit. He was a techno based Knight.<br /> <br /> One thing that tends to keep them apart is that Changeling politics and activities tend to lead mages down the path of madness and Traditionalist tend to attract Technocrats, which are banal as hell (mostly due to their determination to stamp out the supernatural and limit the world to one specific way of looking at the world.) so while some tradition mages with the right paradime might get along great with the fae, the two groups just try to avoid each other for practical reasons. that's my interpretation anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","user":"DeeDee","date":". 12-06-2015, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T00:25:13-08:00","id":781593,"title":"","content":"Freeholds and Glens has a mixed chantry/Freehold it seems to work out ok for the group. It includes the rote needed to self enchant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:39:08-08:00","id":781895,"title":"","content":"I run a mixed game. It works. The current Big Bad is a Marauder who thinks he's sidhe and who's been drawing Technocratic attention towards a mixed node/freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T04:16:14-08:00","id":782215,"title":"","content":"One of the old <b>Changeling</b> supplements (<i>Freeholds and Hidden Glens</i>) had Terabithea, a UC-Santa Cruz freehold/node held jointly by changelings and a cabal of mages (mainly Verbena). So cooperation is certainly plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:16:37-08:00","id":782334,"title":"","content":"It boggles my mind that Changelings would use the name Terabithia as a positive name. Talk about sucking the magic out of childhood...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:44:19-08:00","id":783344,"title":"","content":"I would think that if a party wanted to go mix between Mages and Changelings, you would have to fix the Glammer issue. Kind of shafts the Changeling players when they can't even use their Fey magic more than one a season, while Mages don't really need any resource to pop off a million spells. The Storyteller would need to make it easier for Changelings to replenish their supply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T03:49:29-08:00","id":783347,"title":"","content":"Just remember to watch the banality rating of each tradition, I think they are listed in the mage storyteller book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:27:12-08:00","id":783431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/781227-changlings-and-trad-mages?p=783347#post783347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remember to watch the banality rating of each tradition, I think they are listed in the mage storyteller book</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they definitely have ratings listed in CtD 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:10:00-08:00","id":783565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/781227-changlings-and-trad-mages?p=783347#post783347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remember to watch the banality rating of each tradition, I think they are listed in the mage storyteller book</div> </div> </div> </div>Those were general rules of thumb. Sure the average hermetic is low Banality. But some would be fairly high. The Sons (and Daughters) of Ether would very wildly. So the high Trad rating means little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:51:21-08:00","id":784441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/781227-changlings-and-trad-mages?p=783344#post783344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that if a party wanted to go mix between Mages and Changelings, you would have to fix the Glammer issue. Kind of shafts the Changeling players when they can't even use their Fey magic more than one a season, while Mages don't really need any resource to pop off a million spells. The Storyteller would need to make it easier for Changelings to replenish their supply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dross is usually an important resource for this reason. Dead chimera can also provide a source of Glamour. But the easiest fix is to scale up the amount of Glamour a freehold can produce, like the Node Background in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}